rvices/Hosted/Industrial_Consents_Stations_Trade/FeatureServer/0', 'service_url': 'https://gis.daera-ni.gov.uk/server/rest/services/Hosted/Industrial_Consents_Stations_Trade/FeatureServer', 'capabilities': ['query'], 'info': {'code_field': 'consent_no', 'class_field': 'ind_type', 'status_field': 'app_status', 'date_field': 'date_open', 'nation': 'Northern Ireland', 'completeness': 'complete', 'completeness_note': "all of Northern Ireland; NIEA's trade discharge consents. Sewage and private domestic discharges aren't in it"}, 'check_url': 'https://gis.daera-ni.gov.uk/server/rest/services/Hosted/Industrial_Consents_Stations_Trade/FeatureServer/0/query?where=1%3D1&returnCountOnly=true&f=json'}, {'protocol': 'landing', 'url': 'https://gis.daera-ni.gov.uk/server/rest/services/Hosted/Industrial_Consents_Stations_Trade/FeatureServer'}], '_ctx': {'publisher': 'Department of Agriculture, Environment and Rural Affairs (DAERA)', 'publisher_type': 'public-body', 'country': 'GB', 'seed_catalog': 'curated:uk-pollution.yaml', 'discovered_via': 'curated'}}, {'kind': 'record', 'id': 'uk-daera-historical-land-use', 'title': 'Historical Land Use Database, Northern Ireland (NIEA)', 'publisher': 'Department of Agriculture, Environment and Rural Affairs (DAERA)', 'publisher_type': 'public-body', 'country': 'GB', 'abstract': "NIEA's record of about 14,600 sites in Northern Ireland that have had a potentially contaminating land use: works, mineral workings, railway land, garages and filling stations, gas works, landfills and waste sites, military sites, airfields and others. Descriptio gives the use in the categories of the government's contaminated land guidance (e.g. 'Gas works: coke works and other coal carbonisation plants'); DBID says which source list it came from (Land Use, Industrial Heritage, WMU waste sites, Defence Heritage, ELVs (end-of-life vehicle sites), Licensed Sites, LQPlanApps, Airfields); Y1834...Y1990s note the use at each historical map date where recorded. Points (one per site). It is a screening list of past uses, not a record of contamination. Fields: class field Descriptio, source field DBID, code field Site_ID. 14,591 features. Completeness: complete (all of Northern Ireland; NIEA's database of recorded past uses. An empty answer means none recorded, not that the land was never used for industry). Fills step 1's Northern Ireland gap (no historic landfill or contaminated land layer there). Layer last edited November 2022. A curated record for UK contamination screening (Tobler, 24 Nov 2026): the publisher's own layer, checked to return features for a bounding box.", 'licence': 'Open Government Licence v3.0: "Contains Ordnance Survey of Northern Ireland information licensed under the Open Government Licence v3.0" (DAERA\'s ArcGIS Online item).', 'landing_page': 'https://www.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=b5f5710384f94bb299239df4a1b032a3', 'bbox': [-8.1407, 54.017, -5.3836, 55.308], 'geometry_type': 'point', 'concepts_hint': ['contaminated-land', 'uk-pollution-pack'], 'endpoints': [{'protocol': 'arcgis-featureserver', 'url': 'https://services-eu1.arcgis.com/kswen6BYexuc1SUk/arcgis/rest/services/HistoricalLanduseDataset/FeatureServer/0', 'service_url': 'https://services-eu1.arcgis.com/kswen6BYexuc1SUk/arcgis/rest/services/HistoricalLanduseDataset/FeatureServer', 'capabilities': ['query'], 'info': {'class_field': 'Descriptio', 'source_field': 'DBID', 'code_field': 'Site_ID', 'class_values': ['Land Use', 'Industrial Heritage', 'WMU', 'Defence Heritage', 'ELVs', 'Licensed Sites', 'LQPlanApps', 'Airfields'], 'nation': 'Northern Ireland', 'completeness': 'complete', 'completeness_note': "all of Northern Ireland; NIEA's database of recorded past uses. An empty answer means none recorded, not that the land was never used for industry", 'data_date': '2022-11-23', 'data_date_source': 'layer editing info'}, 'check_url': 'https://services-eu1.arcgis.com/kswen6BYexuc1SUk/arcgis/rest/services/HistoricalLanduseDataset/FeatureServer/0/query?whe